Deliberately empty.

Vercel checks its static output directory before it applies a rewrite, so
whatever sits here is served instead of being forwarded to the VM. Pointing
`outputDirectory` at the repo root would publish the server source — this repo
is private, and that would have quietly made half of it public.

An empty directory means every path misses the filesystem and falls through to
the rewrite in vercel.json, which is the whole intent. Do not put files here.
